```
KEY POINTS:
- ORM = write Python instead of raw SQL to talk to database
- Post.objects = Django's manager — gateway to all DB operations
- create() = creates AND saves in one step
- save() = saves object to database (must call after changing attributes)
- all() = get all records — returns QuerySet
- get() = get ONE record — crashes if not found or multiple found
- filter() = get matching records — returns empty QuerySet if not found
- exclude() = opposite of filter
- exists() = returns True/False — faster than filter() for checking
- count() = returns total number of records
- order_by('field') = ascending, order_by('-field') = descending
- [:5] = limit results (Python slice)
- filter().update() = bulk update without fetching objects
- delete() = remove from database permanently
- QuerySets are LAZY = no DB query until evaluated
- chaining = filter().filter().order_by()[:5] = one DB query

FIELD LOOKUPS:
__exact = exact match
__iexact = case-insensitive exact
__contains = contains (case-sensitive)
__icontains = contains (case-insensitive)
__gt = greater than
__gte = greater than or equal
__lt = less than
__lte = less than or equal
__in = in list
__startswith = starts with
__endswith = ends with
```

---

```python
# QUICK REFERENCE CODE

from blog.models import Post

# CREATE
p1 = Post.objects.create(title="First", content="Hello", is_published=True)
p2 = Post(title="Second", content="World")
p2.save()

# READ
Post.objects.all()                              # all records
Post.objects.get(id=1)                          # one record — crashes if not found
Post.objects.filter(is_published=True)          # matching records — safe
Post.objects.first()                            # first record
Post.objects.last()                             # last record
Post.objects.count()                            # total count
Post.objects.filter(title="x").exists()         # True/False

# FILTER WITH LOOKUPS
Post.objects.filter(title__icontains="django")  # case-insensitive contains
Post.objects.filter(views_count__gt=10)         # greater than
Post.objects.filter(id__in=[1, 2, 3])          # in list
Post.objects.exclude(is_published=True)         # opposite of filter

# ORDER AND LIMIT
Post.objects.all().order_by('-created_at')      # newest first
Post.objects.all().order_by('created_at')       # oldest first
Post.objects.all()[:5]                          # first 5 results

# UPDATE
post = Post.objects.get(id=1)
post.title = "New Title"
post.save()                                     # save after changing

Post.objects.filter(is_published=False).update(views_count=0)  # bulk update

# DELETE
post = Post.objects.get(id=1)
post.delete()                                   # single delete

Post.objects.filter(is_published=False).delete()  # bulk delete

# CHAIN QUERYSETS
Post.objects.filter(
    is_published=True
).filter(
    views_count__gt=10
).order_by('-created_at')[:5]
```

